  "note": "Schematic routes and approximate places drawn for the original Orbis stories; for orientation only. Cables: Around 600 cables are active or planned (TeleGeography). Routes here are schematic and a small sample. Cable faults: about 150–200 per year, mostly from fishing and anchors (International Cable Protection Committee). Chokepoints: Oil flows from the US Energy Information Administration (World Oil Transit Chokepoints; Hormuz ≈ 20 million barrels/day in 2024, Malacca ≈ 23 million in 2023). Trade share and Red Sea disruption: UNCTAD, 2024. Routes are schematic; distances are computed along the drawn line. Phone supply chain: An illustrative, typical smartphone supply chain. Specific suppliers and shares vary by brand and model and change every year. Minerals: Mine production shares ≈ 2023, US Geological Survey Mineral Commodity Summaries 2024, rounded. Refining shares ≈ IEA Global Critical Minerals Outlook 2024. China export controls: gallium and germanium (2023), graphite (2023), selected rare earths (2025). Remittance corridors: World Bank Migration and Development Brief 40 (2024): ≈ USD 656 billion to low- and middle-income countries in 2023, larger than FDI and official aid combined (excl. China). Shares of GDP ≈ 2023, rounded. Flows drawn are major corridors, schematic. Breakfast: Shares rounded and approximate: Côte d'Ivoire ≈ 40% of world cocoa; Brazil the largest coffee producer and ≈ 3/4 of orange-juice exports; Ecuador the largest banana exporter (FAO, ICCO, USDA). Northwest Passage: September Arctic sea-ice minimum ≈ 7 million km² around 1980 vs ≈ 3.4 million in 2012 (record low), NSIDC. Ice is drawn as a circle of equal area, schematic. Routes schematic; distances computed along the drawn line.",
